#### Explanation of the Program

- `Vehicle` is an abstract class because `rentalCharge()` is a pure virtual function.
- `Bicycle`, `TwoWheeler`, `Car`, and `ElectricCar` implement their own rental charge calculations.
- `ElectricBus` is added as a new derived class without modifying the existing classes.
- `Vehicle* fleet[]` stores pointers to different vehicle types.
- Runtime polymorphism calls the appropriate `rentalCharge()` function.
- `rent()` changes the status of the vehicle to rented.
- `returnVehicle()` calculates the rental charge and late fee, then changes the status to available.

